=3D"true">On this page</button></div><div class=3D"theme-doc-markdown markd=
own"><header><h1>Calico quickstart guide</h1></header>
<p>This quickstart guide shows you how to install Calico, secure a cluster =
with network policy, and monitor network traffic with Calico Whisker.</p>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_yhof" id=3D"before-you-begin">=
Before you begin<a href=3D"https://docs.tigera.io/calico/latest/getting-sta=
rted/kubernetes/quickstart#before-you-begin" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=
=3D"Direct link to Before you begin" title=3D"Direct link to Before you beg=
in" translate=3D"no">=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<p>You'll need to install a few tools to complete this tutorial:</p>
<ul>
<li class=3D""><code>kind</code>.
This is what you'll use to create a cluster on your workstation.
For installation instructions, see the <a href=3D"https://kind.sigs.k8s.io/=
docs/user/quick-start/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" class=
=3D""><code>kind</code> documentation</a>.</li>
<li class=3D"">Docker Engine or Docker Desktop.
This is required to run containers for the <code>kind</code> utility.
For installation instructions, see the <a href=3D"https://docs.docker.com/d=
esktop/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" class=3D"">Docker do=
cumentation</a>.</li>
<li class=3D""><code>kubectl</code>.
This is the tool you'll use to interact with your cluster.
For installation instructions, see the <a href=3D"https://kubernetes.io/doc=
s/tasks/tools/#kubectl" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" class=
=3D"">Kubernetes documentation</a></li>
</ul>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_yhof" id=3D"step-1-create-a-cl=
uster">Step 1: Create a cluster<a href=3D"https://docs.tigera.io/calico/lat=
est/getting-started/kubernetes/quickstart#step-1-create-a-cluster" class=3D=
"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Step 1: Create a cluster" title=3D=
"Direct link to Step 1: Create a cluster" translate=3D"no">=E2=80=8B</a></h=
2>
<p>In this step, you will:</p>
<ul>
<li class=3D""><strong>Create a cluster:</strong> Use <code>kind</code> to =
create a Kubernetes cluster.</li>
<li class=3D""><strong>Verify the cluster:</strong> Check that the cluster =
is running and ready.</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li class=3D"">
<p>Create a file called <code>config.yaml</code> and give it the following =
content:</p>
<div data-codeblock-validation=3D"true"><div class=3D"language-bash codeBlo=
ckContainer_bgB3 theme-code-block" style=3D"--prism-color: #393A34; --prism=
-background-color: #f6f8fa;"><div class=3D"codeBlockContent_vsYo"><pre tabi=
ndex=3D"0" class=3D"prism-code language-bash codeBlock_5KcV thin-scrollbar"=
 style=3D"color: rgb(57, 58, 52); background-color: rgb(246, 248, 250);"><c=
ode class=3D"codeBlockLines_vfFu"><span class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color=
: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span class=3D"token plain">kind: Cluster</span><br></s=
pan><span class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span clas=
s=3D"token plain">apiVersion: kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4</span><br></span><span=
 class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span class=3D"toke=
n plain">nodes:</span><br></span><span class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color:=
 rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span class=3D"token plain">  - role: control-plane</spa=
n><br></span><span class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><=
span class=3D"token plain">  - role: worker</span><br></span><span class=3D=
"token-line" style=3D"color: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span class=3D"token plain">=
  - role: worker</span><br></span><span class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color=
: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span class=3D"token plain">networking:</span><br></spa=
n><span class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span class=
=3D"token plain">  disableDefaultCNI: true</span><br></span><span class=3D"=
token-line" style=3D"color: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span class=3D"token plain"> =
 podSubnet: 192.168.0.0/16</span><br></span></code></pre><div class=3D"butt=
onGroup_a65Q"><button type=3D"button" aria-label=3D"Copy code to clipboard"=
 title=3D"Copy" class=3D"clean-btn" data-faitracker-form-bind=3D"true"><spa=
n class=3D"copyButtonIcons_jj7A" aria-hidden=3D"true"><svg viewBox=3D"0 0 2=
4 24" class=3D"copyButtonIcon_nwTv"><path fill=3D"currentColor" d=3D"M19,21=
H8V7H19M19,5H8A2,2 0 0,0 6,7V21A2,2 0 0,0 8,23H19A2,2 0 0,0 21,21V7A2,2 0 0=
,0 19,5M16,1H4A2,2 0 0,0 2,3V17H4V3H16V1Z"></path></svg><svg viewBox=3D"0 0=
 24 24" class=3D"copyButtonSuccessIcon_pql8"><path fill=3D"currentColor" d=
=3D"M21,7L9,19L3.5,13.5L4.91,12.09L9,16.17L19.59,5.59L21,7Z"></path></svg><=
/span></button></div></div></div></div>
<p>This configuration file tells <code>kind</code> to create a cluster with=
 one control-plane node and two worker nodes.
It instructs <code>kind</code> to create the cluster without a CNI.
The <code>podSubnet</code> range defines the IP addresses that Kubernetes w=
ill use for pods.</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"">
<p>Start your Kubernetes cluster with the configuration file by running the=
 following command:</p>
<div data-codeblock-validation=3D"true"><div class=3D"language-bash codeBlo=
ckContainer_bgB3 theme-code-block" style=3D"--prism-color: #393A34; --prism=
-background-color: #f6f8fa;"><div class=3D"codeBlockContent_vsYo"><pre tabi=
ndex=3D"0" class=3D"prism-code language-bash codeBlock_5KcV thin-scrollbar"=
 style=3D"color: rgb(57, 58, 52); background-color: rgb(246, 248, 250);"><c=
ode class=3D"codeBlockLines_vfFu"><span class=3D"token-line" style=3D"color=
: rgb(57, 58, 52);"><span class=3D"token plain">kind create cluster --name=
=3Dcalico-cluster --config=3Dconfig.yaml</span><br></span></code></pre><div=
 class=3D"buttonGroup_a65Q"><button type=3D"button" aria-label=3D"Copy code=
 to clipboard" title=3D"Copy" class=3D"clean-btn" data-faitracker-form-bind=
